 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Bundle routes are recorded as deferred callbacks and replayed onto the app at registration time. The relevant code is in `src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py` unless noted.\n\n1. **Recording**: `Bundle.attach_route_rule` (413) does not touch an app. It calls `Bundle.record` (224), which appends a lambda to `deferred_functions`. The route decorators (`route`, etc.) go through this method.\n2. **Registering**: `App.register_bundle` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:571`) calls `Bundle.register(app, options)` (273).\n3. **Replaying**:\n   - `register` stores the bundle in `app.bundles[name]`.\n   - It builds a `BundleSetupState` via `make_setup_state` (246).\n   - It calls `_merge_bundle_funcs` (379), which copies the view functions, error handlers and request hooks into the app.\n   - It runs each deferred function with the state (334–335).\n4. **Attaching to the app**: `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule` (87) applies `url_prefix` and `subdomain`, merges `url_defaults`, and prefixes the endpoint with `{name_prefix}.{name}.`. It then calls `self.app.attach_route_rule(...)` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:606`).\n5. **Nested bundles**: `register` recurses into `self._bundles` (349–377), combining the prefixes and subdomains before calling `bundle.register` again.",
